My personal opinion on this is: The main reason why Mandrake won't be

releasing a version in the (near) future is because the alpha market is

quite small.

> > Thanks for your prompt reply.

 

> Again, I'm going to defer to the guys still working on it. There are still

> people working on cooker, and in fact ALO has donated a machine for this a

> well. So the develpoment work is being done, just outside Mandrake Soft.

Some people participating in the effort are with Mandrakesoft, some

aren't. I beleive most (if not all) of the effort is being done in our

"free" time, but most Mandrake hackers are very friendly & polite to put

in a modification / patch / bugfix to get things working on the alpha,

as long as it doesn't interfere with the other (mainly x86) ports.

Here's an un-official peice of html I put up to describe the effort a

bit:

http://d10179.upc-d.chello.nl/~stefan/mandrake-alpha.html

If you're interested to join, you're welcome. ;-)

Stefan van der Eijk

